WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:17.689
next morning, the Tornadoes met at the Donovans' tree house.

2
00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:22.792
"We can find the oldest gravestone in the cemetery," said Laura.

3
00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:26.314
"But where will we find the oldest person?"

4
00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.516
"Maybe at the Willow Creek Senior Home," said Joy.

5
00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:32.509
"Lots of old people live there."

6
00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.814
"We can get a calendar of community events at the library," said Carlos.

7
00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:41.917
"But how will we find a town law?"

8
00:00:42.398 --> 00:00:43.078
asked Joy.

9
00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:46.221
She looked down at the list and frowned.

10
00:00:46.241 --> 00:00:49.504
"We have less than two weeks to find all this stuff."

11
00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:51.686
"I can help!"

12
00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:52.867
said Manny.

13
00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:56.690
"No. You can't," said Carlos.

14
00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.151
"You're a baby."

15
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.121
"He can count, right?"

16
00:01:01.521 --> 00:01:02.181
said Joy.

17
00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:08.183
"We have to count stop signs, mailboxes, and streetlamps on Main Street."

18
00:01:08.203 --> 00:01:11.065
"I can count to a hundred!"

19
00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:12.185
said Manny.

20
00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:15.166
"Good enough," said Joy.

21
00:01:16.307 --> 00:01:19.668
Just then a gray cloud drifted through the tree house.

22
00:01:20.908 --> 00:01:21.889
Laura coughed.

23
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.110
Carlos sniffed the air.

24
00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.492
"I smell smoke," he said.

25
00:01:30.612 --> 00:01:33.174
The Tornadoes looked out of the tree house window.

26
00:01:33.194 --> 00:01:35.455
"Hey, Grandpa!"

27
00:01:35.836 --> 00:01:36.536
Joy yelled.

28
00:01:37.037 --> 00:01:38.017
"What are you doing?"

29
00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:40.459
Grandpa looked up.

30
00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:42.741
"Oh, hey, kids," he said.

31
00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:44.782
"I'm just burning a few weeds."

32
00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:47.884
He poked at his fire with a stick.

33
00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:52.407
A glowing leaf floated up and landed in dry grass.

34
00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:54.609
A flame shot up.

35
00:01:55.169 --> 00:01:58.992
"Oops," said Grandpa and smashed the flame with his boot.

36
00:02:00.276 --> 00:02:02.758
"There goes another one," said Carlos.

37
00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:05.580
Grandpa smashed another little flame.

38
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.582
"And there's one," said Joy.

39
00:02:09.102 --> 00:02:10.383
Grandpa stamped again.

40
00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:14.005
Suddenly there were little flames everywhere.

41
00:02:15.246 --> 00:02:18.288
Grandpa was running in a panic, stamping his feet.

42
00:02:23.471 --> 00:02:24.172
said Manny.

43
00:02:24.732 --> 00:02:27.054
The kids hurried down the tree house steps.

44
00:02:28.355 --> 00:02:30.036
"Get a bucket from the back porch!"

45
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.421
Grandpa yelled.

46
00:02:32.582 --> 00:02:33.983
The Tornadoes took off.

47
00:02:34.484 --> 00:02:38.727
But by the time they ran back up the hill, the fire was blazing.

48
00:02:39.949 --> 00:02:41.810
Smoke sailed into the sky.

49
00:02:43.151 --> 00:02:46.294
Grandpa grabbed the bucket and dipped it in the pond.

50
00:02:47.475 --> 00:02:51.138
He threw water on the fire, but the fire kept growing.

51
00:02:52.359 --> 00:02:53.640
Then they heard sirens.

52
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.882
"Fire trucks!"

53
00:02:56.423 --> 00:02:57.344
shouted Carlos.

54
00:02:58.524 --> 00:03:02.346
The fire chief's truck was in front and the fire engine followed.

55
00:03:03.446 --> 00:03:06.327
They roared up the driveway and across the field.

56
00:03:07.728 --> 00:03:11.650
Three firefighters jumped out and unrolled the fire hose.

57
00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.490
"Get back!"

58
00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.452
the fire chief called to Grandpa and the kids.

59
00:03:17.812 --> 00:03:21.033
Water whooshed out of the hose and onto the fire.

60
00:03:22.294 --> 00:03:26.996
Soon there was just a circle of wet, black grass where the fire had been.

61
00:03:28.136 --> 00:03:29.017
"What happened here?"

62
00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:30.538
asked the fire chief.

63
00:03:31.779 --> 00:03:33.380
Her name was Rita Carlson.

64
00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.563
She had been a Willow Creek firefighter for 15 years.

65
00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:43.407
"Well," said Grandpa, "I was just burning a few weeds.

66
00:03:43.707 --> 00:03:45.208
Then the fire went everywhere.

67
00:03:46.509 --> 00:03:51.572
When the kids got here with the bucket—" Chief Carlson interrupted Grandpa.

68
00:03:51.592 --> 00:03:55.635
"So you didn't have anything ready to control your fire?"

69
00:03:56.075 --> 00:03:56.656
she asked.

70
00:03:58.016 --> 00:04:00.218
"I guess not," said Grandpa.

71
00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:03.000
The fire chief frowned.

72
00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.882
"May I see your burning permit, Mr.

73
00:04:05.902 --> 00:04:09.344
Donovan?" "Burning permit?"

74
00:04:09.844 --> 00:04:10.725
said Grandpa.

75
00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:13.307
Chief Carlson sighed.

76
00:04:13.327 --> 00:04:20.892
"Mr. Donovan, Willow Creek's burning law requires you to get a burning permit before starting a fire.

77
00:04:21.933 --> 00:04:23.234
You have broken that law."

78
00:04:23.254 --> 00:04:26.216
"Hooray!" cried Joy.

79
00:04:27.524 --> 00:04:29.004
Everyone stared at Joy.

80
00:04:29.024 --> 00:04:31.825
"That's just what we're looking for!"

81
00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.086
she explained.

82
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.186
"A law for our scavenger hunt!

83
00:04:36.687 --> 00:04:39.247
Do you have a copy of the burning law, Chief Carlson?"

84
00:04:40.748 --> 00:04:44.789
"Oh! We need a list of fire-safety tips too," said Laura.

85
00:04:44.809 --> 00:04:48.070
"No problem," said Chief Carlson.

86
00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:51.030
"I have both of those things in my truck.

87
00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.551
And for you, Mr.

88
00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.691
Donovan, I have a fine."

89
00:04:55.852 --> 00:04:56.852
Grandpa frowned.

90
00:04:57.324 --> 00:04:58.806
But the Tornadoes cheered.

91
00:05:00.068 --> 00:05:05.455
The fire trucks were just leaving when Katie came racing down Blackberry Road on her bike.

92
00:05:05.475 --> 00:05:07.738
"Here comes an Earthworm!"

93
00:05:08.198 --> 00:05:08.999
said Carlos.

94
00:05:09.019 --> 00:05:11.302
"Don't tell her what we found!"

95
00:05:12.203 --> 00:05:15.668
The Tornadoes laughed and put two check marks on their list.
